{
  "$defs": {
    "CdsConventionKey": {
      "description": "Key to look up CDS conventions (Currency + DocClause).\n\nCDS conventions are identified by both currency and documentation clause, as different\nclauses have different market conventions. Used to look up [`CdsConventionSpec`](crate::market::conventions::defs::CdsConventionSpec)\nfrom the convention registry.\n\n# Examples\n\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_valuations::market::conventions::ids::{CdsConventionKey, CdsDocClause};\nuse finstack_quant_core::currency::Currency;\n\nlet key = CdsConventionKey {\n    currency: Currency::USD,\n    doc_clause: CdsDocClause::Cr14,\n};\n```",
      "properties": {
        "currency": {
          "$ref": "https://finstack_quant.dev/schemas/common/1/currency.schema.json",
          "description": "The currency of the CDS."
        },
        "doc_clause": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CdsDocClause",
          "description": "The documentation clause (e.g. CR14, MM14)."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "currency",
        "doc_clause"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CdsDocClause": {
      "description": "CDS market standard documentation clauses.\n\nRepresents the ISDA documentation clause used for CDS contracts. Different clauses\ndefine different restructuring events and settlement procedures. Used as part of\n[`CdsConventionKey`] to look up CDS conventions.\n\n# Examples\n\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_valuations::market::conventions::ids::CdsDocClause;\n\nlet clause = CdsDocClause::Cr14; // Cum-Restructuring 2014\n```",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "cr14",
          "description": "Cum-Restructuring 2014 (CR14)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "mr14",
          "description": "Modified-Restructuring 2014 (MR14)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "mm14",
          "description": "Modified-Modified-Restructuring 2014 (MM14)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "xr14",
          "description": "No-Restructuring 2014 (XR14)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "isda_na",
          "description": "ISDA North American Corporate (IsdaNa)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "isda_eu",
          "description": "ISDA European Corporate (IsdaEu)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "isda_as",
          "description": "ISDA Asia Corporate (IsdaAs)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "isda_au",
          "description": "ISDA Australia Corporate (IsdaAu)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "isda_nz",
          "description": "ISDA New Zealand Corporate (IsdaNz)",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "custom",
          "description": "Custom / Other",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "InflationSwapConventionId": {
      "description": "Identifier for Inflation Swap market conventions (e.g., \"USD-CPI\", \"UK-RPI\").\n\nUsed to look up [`InflationSwapConventions`](crate::market::conventions::defs::InflationSwapConventions)\nfrom the convention registry.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "IrFutureContractId": {
      "description": "Stable identifier for an Interest Rate Future contract (e.g., \"CME:SR3\").\n\nUsed to look up [`IrFutureConventions`](crate::market::conventions::defs::IrFutureConventions)\nfrom the convention registry.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "OptionType": {
      "description": "Option payoff direction used by analytical and numerical model engines.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "call",
          "description": "Call option.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "put",
          "description": "Put option.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Pillar": {
      "description": "The maturity pillar of a quote.\n\nThe pillar represents the maturity of the instrument referenced by the quote. OTC instruments\n(swaps, deposits) typically use `Tenor` (e.g., \"5Y\") to allow rolling headers that automatically\nadjust as the valuation date changes. Futures or bespoke runs may use `Date` to pin a specific\nmaturity date.\n\nThe JSON wire form is externally tagged: `{\"tenor\": {\"count\": 5, \"unit\": \"years\"}}`\nor `{\"date\": \"2029-06-20\"}`. A bare string such as `\"5Y\"` is rejected.\n\n# Examples\n\nUsing a tenor pillar:\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_calibration::quotes::ids::Pillar;\n\n# fn example() -> finstack_quant_core::Result<()> {\nlet pillar = Pillar::Tenor(\"5Y\".parse()?);\n# Ok(())\n# }\n```\n\nUsing a date pillar:\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_calibration::quotes::ids::Pillar;\nuse finstack_quant_core::dates::Date;\n\nlet pillar = Pillar::Date(Date::from_calendar_date(2029, time::Month::June, 20).unwrap());\n```",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A relative tenor (e.g., 5Y, 3M).\n\nThe maturity is calculated relative to the valuation date, allowing quotes to \"roll\"\nforward automatically. This is the standard approach for OTC instruments.",
          "properties": {
            "tenor": {
              "$ref": "https://finstack_quant.dev/schemas/common/1/tenor.schema.json"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "tenor"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "An absolute date.\n\nThe maturity is fixed to a specific date, regardless of the valuation date. This is\ntypically used for futures contracts or bespoke instruments with fixed maturities.",
          "properties": {
            "date": {
              "$ref": "https://finstack_quant.dev/schemas/common/1/date.schema.json"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "date"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    },
    "QuoteId": {
      "description": "A stable identifier for a market quote (e.g., \"USD-OIS-SWAP-5Y\").\n\nThis ID is used for human readability, logging, and potentially matching against external\ndata sources. Quote IDs should be unique within a calibration set and follow a consistent\nnaming convention (e.g., \"{currency}-{index}-{type}-{pillar}\").\n\n[`QuoteId::new`] is infallible, including for empty strings. Empty or\nwhitespace-only IDs are rejected when this type is deserialized from the\nwire, and again by [`MarketQuote::validate`](super::market_quote::MarketQuote::validate).\n\n# Examples\n\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_calibration::quotes::ids::QuoteId;\n\nlet id = QuoteId::new(\"USD-SOFR-DEP-1M\");\nassert_eq!(id.as_str(), \"USD-SOFR-DEP-1M\");\n```",
      "minLength": 1,
      "pattern": ".*\\S.*",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "SwaptionConventionId": {
      "description": "Identifier for Swaption market conventions (e.g., \"USD\", \"EUR\").\n\nUsed to look up [`SwaptionConventions`](crate::market::conventions::defs::SwaptionConventions)\nfrom the convention registry.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "VolQuoteType": {
      "description": "Quoting convention of the volatilities stored on a [`VolSurface`].\n\nThe same `vol_surface_id` channel is read by consumers with very different\nexpectations: rates calibrations typically read normal (Bachelier, absolute)\nvols on an `expiry × tenor` ATM matrix, while equity/FX/swaption smile\nconsumers read Black (lognormal, relative) vols on `expiry × strike`. The\nstored numbers are an order of magnitude apart (e.g. 0.008 normal vs 0.20\nBlack), so misreading one as the other silently mis-prices. Tagging the\nquote type lets consumers enforce their convention via\n[`VolSurface::require_quote_type`].",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "black_lognormal",
          "description": "Black (lognormal) implied volatility, relative units (the default).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "normal",
          "description": "Normal (Bachelier) implied volatility, absolute rate units.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "XccyConventionId": {
      "description": "Identifier for cross-currency swap market conventions (e.g., \"EUR/USD-XCCY\").",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "$id": "https://finstack_quant.dev/schemas/market/1/market_quote.schema.json",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "Canonical tagged market quote.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "class": "rates",
      "id": "USD-SOFR-DEP-1M",
      "index": "USD-SOFR",
      "pillar": {
        "tenor": {
          "count": 1,
          "unit": "months"
        }
      },
      "rate": 0.0525,
      "type": "deposit"
    }
  ],
